{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/191","id":4536732191,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQmfsR88AAAABDmkKHw","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/191","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/191.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/191.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/191","number":191,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Harden CI pipeline verdicts and process cleanup","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Compute broken-link recovery from the complete Lychee report, so a recovered transient failure cannot hide an answered failure such as a 404. The terminal link step also avoids repainting an explicitly cancelled run.\n- Require both platform digest artifacts before manifest creation, then read back both `latest` and the version tag and require `linux/amd64` plus `linux/arm64` on each.\n- Classify cancelled jobs against their effective workflow concurrency policy. Only a moved branch plus literal `cancel-in-progress: true` is excused; `false`, missing groups/jobs, expressions, and unreadable configuration fail closed.\n- Keep budget-wrapper state separate from a command's temporary directory, observe the full process group via `ps`, retry signals through passwordless `sudo`, report survivors, and relay captured stdout/stderr so descendants cannot hold the CI pipe open.\n- Bracket every contributor- or operator-authored changeset body with a fresh unpredictable 128-bit GitHub Actions `stop-commands` token.\n- Refresh the vulnerable transitive development resolutions reported by the current npm advisory database.\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\nThe automated regressions cover each reported failure mode:\n\n- mixed `[404]` plus recovered `[ERROR]` Lychee report remains failing;\n- manifest creation requires exactly two digests and both published tags are inspected for both target platforms;\n- a moved branch excuses a cancellable link job but still fails a non-cancellable publish job and an expression-valued policy;\n- a detached descendant cannot hold the wrapper's output pipe open, an ignored `SIGTERM` reaches `SIGKILL`, privileged-survivor handling is present, and a command that clears `TMPDIR` still exits successfully;\n- a changeset containing `##[error]` is emitted only between fresh stop/resume markers;\n- the PR adds exactly one valid patch changeset.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `npm ci`\n- `npm test` — 466 passed\n- `bun test` — 466 passed\n- `deno test --allow-read` — 367 passed\n- `npm run check`\n- `npm --prefix examples/universal-app run build`\n- `docker run --rm -v \"$PWD:/repo\" -w /repo rhysd/actionlint:1.7.12 -color`\n- root and example-app `npm audit --package-lock-only --audit-level=high` — 0 vulnerabilities\n- `bash -n scripts/check-pipeline-status.sh scripts/read-job-cancel-in-progress.sh scripts/run-with-budget-warning.sh`\n- GitHub Actions — 37 checks passed across all five workflows (10 intentional skips)\n\n## Implementation research\n\nThe solution follows GitHub's documented fresh-token workflow-command bracket, per-job concurrency semantics, and runner temporary-directory contract, plus Docker Buildx's registry manifest inspection behavior. The production-tested `link-foundation/box` shell components referenced by the issues were compared and adapted to this repository. No new runtime library was needed; the implementation uses the existing Node, Bash, Python, `ps`, and Docker Buildx tooling.\n\nFixes #190\n\nFixes #184\n\nFixes #185\n\nFixes #186\n\nFixes #187\n\nFixes #188\n\nFixes #189\n","created_at":"2026-09-15T12:03:20Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T16:23:56Z","closed_at":"2026-09-15T16:23:56Z","merged_at":"2026-09-15T16:23:56Z","merge_commit_sha":"e4f23d74e6679c24b584980977c74ab631f41576","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pip